+## Deploy: Vercel frontend + hosted backend
+
+Vercel runs the **web UI and a thin proxy**; the Python backend needs a persistent disk (SQLite index, Qdrant data,
+the cloned repo), long-running indexing and a background watcher, none of which fit serverless functions, so it
+runs on a container host (Render, Railway, Fly.io, or any VPS). Streamlit remains the local/dev UI.
+
+```
+Browser ──► Vercel (web/index.html + web/api/[...path].js) ──► GitContext backend (Docker) ──► Qdrant + SQLite on disk
+              static UI, hides BACKEND_URL / API key             FastAPI, x-api-key auth, auto-index + auto-sync
+```
+
+**1. Deploy the backend** (any Docker host; `render.yaml` is a ready blueprint, `docker compose up` also works):
+
+| Backend env var | Purpose |
+|---|---|
+| `GITCONTEXT_REPO` | repo to index (URL, `owner/name`) |
+| `GITCONTEXT_API_KEY` | shared secret; every endpoint except `/health` and the HMAC webhook requires `x-api-key` |
+| `GITCONTEXT_AUTO_INDEX_ON_START=true` | index in the background on first boot |
+| `GITCONTEXT_AUTO_SYNC_SECONDS=300` | poll the repo and re-index changed files |
+| `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, `GITHUB_TOKEN` | answers; PRs/issues/incidents and private repos |
+| `GITCONTEXT_CORS_ORIGINS` | only if the browser calls the backend directly (not needed with the proxy) |
+| `GITCONTEXT_WEBHOOK_SECRET` | optional: point a GitHub webhook (push, pull_request, issues) at `https://<backend>/webhook/github` for instant re-indexing |
+
+Mount a persistent volume at `/data`, give it enough RAM for the local ONNX embedding model (1–2 GB), and note that the
+first boot downloads the repo and embeds it (minutes, depending on size and CPU). Check progress at `/status`.
+
+**2. Deploy the frontend on Vercel**
+
+1. Import this repo in Vercel and set **Root Directory** to `web` (Framework Preset: *Other*; no build command).
+   Or from a terminal: `cd web && npx vercel --prod`.
+2. Add environment variables to the Vercel project:
+
+   | Vercel env var | Value |
+   |---|---|
+   | `BACKEND_URL` | `https://<your-backend-host>` (no trailing path) |
+   | `BACKEND_API_KEY` | the same value as the backend's `GITCONTEXT_API_KEY` |
+   | `ALLOW_ADMIN` | leave unset. `true` exposes `/sync` and `/index` to anyone who can open the site |
+
+3. Redeploy and open the Vercel URL. The status pill shows fresh / stale / not indexed.
+
+**Security notes.** The Vercel site is public by default: anyone with the URL can ask questions, which spends your LLM
+credits. Turn on Vercel *Deployment Protection* (password / SSO) or add rate limiting before sharing it. The proxy only
+forwards `health`, `status`, `query` and `search`, caps request size, and never sends `BACKEND_URL` or the key to the
+browser. `vercel.json` sets `maxDuration: 60` for the proxy; confirm that fits your Vercel plan's limits.
+
+**Tests for this part:** `cd web && npm install && npm test`: proxy behaviour against a mock backend, and the page
+rendered in jsdom (including that model/repo text cannot inject HTML).
+
